            {
                "entry_id": "bad0a5ce-955a-3114-8675-75e548be4419",
                "word": "Romaine",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a1c5dedf-a419-4c17-b9da-4d39aaf57f43",
                        "entry_id": "bad0a5ce-955a-3114-8675-75e548be4419",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Romaines"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                        "entry_id": "bad0a5ce-955a-3114-8675-75e548be4419",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative letter-case form of romaine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "49a184ad-2cc3-4541-8387-f4a4fff8a7f5",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "In February, I’d made and frozen a pork ragout. With penne pasta and a Romaine salad with vinaigrette, it would be perfect. […] Finally, I located the penne, washed and dried the Romaine leaves, and whisked together a Dijon vinaigrette."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d42237a5-b5fd-4a07-93a5-dd265e7bdddd",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "Serve shrimp with sauce on a bed of Romaine leaves, if desired."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94b57d31-72c1-4831-80cb-e28ac1bd5699",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "Tear the Romaine leaves into irregular bite-sized pieces. (If using store-bought Romaine, remove the tough, watery rib in each leaf.)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03e9eae8-febf-4e5a-8a10-1228523fa7dc",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "Drizzle a little of the salad dressing over the Cos or Romaine leaves around the 4 serving bowls."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf2098b9-3895-47af-8847-6f4b4ca7564c",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "A garlicky Caesar is a nice starter with whole Romaine leaves and crispy sourdough croutons, but most can’t resist the creamy, but very rich, signature lobster soup."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6496aca-3661-4396-8e43-05436bdfb4e6",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "Toss the Romaine leaves with dressing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec4b4e21-8a98-4ada-a9b7-f4b36045251e",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "When the seedlings begin to crowd one another, thin to four inches apart for smaller-leaf lettuces and up to twelve inches apart for larger varieties and head lettuces such as robust Romaines, which prefer wider spacing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1fd05f20-72a7-4b8a-8b89-00ecb09e8cec",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "I like to have watercress to soften into the roast gravy, and crisp baby gem or Romaine leaves to catch and contrast with the gravy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c4216a4-4b86-4d11-a592-054c64bdd2fd",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "She starts tearing the Romaine leaves into bite-size pieces and adding them to the bowl."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4f77ad1-1dc8-420e-badd-7346da3d114e",
                                "sense_id": "a8f98794-da96-3c6c-a725-5a9e4a8c230d",
                                "text": "[…] served with a side salad of 1 cup chopped Romaine, 5 halved cherry tomatoes, 1 Tbsp. chopped green onions, with olive oil and vinegar dressing"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
